From 4d1c0b7e9a2f5836c07b1d4e8f3a6b9520c7e14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: therealmharc <therealmharc@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:55:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Disable the HAL LeicaFilter pipeline

Every capture or recording that has a Leica filter selected takes
camerahalserver down.  The HAL builds its FilterPlugin pipeline as soon
as the app sets the filter tag, and the heap it works on comes back
corrupted: tombstones land in unrelated places each run (mialgoengine,
micamera_hal_core ImageTarget::releaseBuffer, mtkcam_streamutils
UsersManager::queryUser_ with a recycled map head, libui
GraphicBuffer, libfeature_vrp checkROI), which is the signature of an
out-of-bounds write rather than one bad pointer.  It is not size
dependent - 4096x3072 crashes as reliably as 5184x3888 - and disabling
AFBC/AFRC on the device does not help, so it is not a stride or
compression issue either.

setCaptureFilterEnable() is the single point that feeds both the
preview-side flag and the capture request tag (z8/r->W3), so forcing it
false keeps the whole FilterPlugin pipeline out of the HAL.  Camera
sessions, captures and recording keep working; the photo just no longer
carries the Leica filter until the vendor side is fixed.
---
 smali/i8/K.smali | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali/i8/K.smali b/smali/i8/K.smali
--- a/smali/i8/K.smali
+++ b/smali/i8/K.smali
@@ -2182,6 +2182,10 @@
 
     invoke-static {v1, v0}, Lcom/android/camera/log/Log;->v(Ljava/lang/String;Ljava/lang/String;)V
 
+    # force the HAL filter path off: camerahalserver corrupts its heap when the
+    # FilterPlugin pipeline is enabled on this port (see 0012 for the LUT side)
+    const/4 p1, 0x0
+
     invoke-virtual {p0}, Li8/K;->d()Ljava/util/Optional;
 
     move-result-object p0
